{
  "0": "Learning objective: add 0.1*mean(softplus(s_neg-s_pos)) to the existing loss, using only the positive and negative scores already computed for each training example. This modest pairwise term may improve top-10 separation without changing sampling or scoring. Preserve features, embeddings, GRU topology, readout, optimizer and training schedule. Apply across all four datasets, training exactly one model per category.",
  "1": "Network architecture: add a narrow residual adapter inside the GRU network, h'=h+0.1*W_up(tanh(W_down(h))), with bottleneck width max(8, hidden_size//4) and zero-initialized W_up. Feed h' into the unchanged history readout and scorer. This starts with baseline behavior while allowing inexpensive nonlinear refinement without another recurrent layer. Preserve features, embeddings, loss and optimizer; reproduce the adapter in the predictor writer. Train one model per category across all four datasets.",
  "2": "Feature construction: multiply each nonpadding input item embedding by 1+0.1*min(log(1+c),log(4))/log(4), where c counts that item's earlier occurrences in the available user prefix. This bounded, parameter-free repeat indicator may distinguish recurring interests without changing item identities or sequence selection. Compute it causally and identically during training and prediction. Preserve embedding tables, GRU topology, readout, scorer, loss and optimizer. Train one model per category across all four datasets.",
  "3": "Training strategy: halve the current learning rate while retaining the optimizer type, batch size, dropout, weight decay and scheduler shape. Smaller updates may reduce the late validation deterioration visible in Electronics while retaining useful recurrent representations in the other categories. Preserve architecture, features, scoring, readout, loss and sampling. Keep preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, epoch cap 200 and existing checkpoint selection; train exactly one model per category across all four datasets."
